Run:      2026-10-20 08:59-09:12 NZDT.  The DUT's Local RADIUS Server was switched on,
          measured on the wire, and removed again.
          The DUT clock runs in UTC, 13 h behind the box; DUT log times below are UTC,
          tool times NZDT.
Bench:    tb277, consoles u2 = swi_d (DUT); Test Engineer bidhanc@bidhanc-dl
Tester:   bench-runner
Graded:   tester
Case:     T33407.  The test-case database holds NO authored objective, NO step text, NO test
          data and NO expected result for this case. Its single step is empty.
          The tester designed the objective and all 7 steps below.
          Objective (designed by the tester), in five parts.
          1. The built-in Local RADIUS Server of the AT-x960-56YSQ can be enabled with a
             NAS client and local users.
          2. It then answers real RADIUS Access-Requests on the wire. A valid user gets an
             Access-Accept. An invalid user gets an Access-Reject.
          3. Every reply is bound to the configured shared secret.
          4. A host that is not a configured NAS gets no answer at all.
          5. The whole configuration can be removed again.
