  Three measured observations:
  1. `nas 127.0.0.1` was NOT configured by this case. The baseline running-config held no
     radius line at all. Turning the Local RADIUS Server on creates this loopback NAS entry
     by itself, with a generated key and `message-authenticator optional`.
  2. The shared key is stored and shown only in encrypted form. The plain text `testing123`
     never appears in any `show` output.
  3. `authentication mac` added no line to the running-config. MAC, EAP-MD5, EAP-TLS and
     EAP-PEAP are already enabled by default, so the command changed nothing.
  => STEP 3 PASS: the server is configured and running. The device reports
     "Server status : Run", 2 NAS entries and 2 users, with every counter still at 0.
     swi_d.cfg was saved at this point.

