  The DUT log names the reason:

    2026 Oct 19 20:10:05 daemon.err awplus radiusd[19826]: Ignoring request to auth address *
      port 1812 bound to server default from unknown client 10.38.22.65 port 55442 proto udp

  The `Unknown NAS` counter stayed at 0. The packet is dropped before the counted path, so
  that counter name is misleading on this platform. This is recorded as an observation, not
  as a defect.
  => STEP 5 PASS: 2 requests went out and 0 replies came back. There was no ICMP port
     unreachable this time, unlike step 1, because the socket IS open. The server simply
     refuses to serve a client that is not in its NAS list.

